A high-resolution version (60k translucent points on dark ground) is saved at `/workspace/attractor.svg` — worth opening in a browser, where the density variations become luminous. To prospect for your own: `python3 attractor.py <any-seed>`. Each seed yields a completely different creature; the Lyapunov filter guarantees you never get a boring one. Seed 13, for instance, produced a dense moth-wing shape that overwhelmed the terminal but would look great as the SVG.

What I like about this little program is that it doesn't just draw chaos — it *certifies* it, by measuring how fast neighboring trajectories fly apart before deeming a picture worth drawing.
